# Explicit, not inherited. Vercel falls back to .gitignore only when this
# file is absent, and 59GB of brand library, retreat photography and video
# now sit inside this folder. Not worth relying on a fallback for.
CydnieJocelyn-Site/
Costa Rica copy/
Family Travel copy/
Fonts copy/
cydniejocelyn/

.git/
.DS_Store

# build output and local tooling, not part of the deployed site
tools/
HANDOFF.md
BRIEF.md
README.md

# Working documents. These are wireframes, briefs and copy decks that arrive
# as folders beside the site, and Vercel serves whatever it is given: the
# build brief was live at /The Build page/files/CLAUDE-CODE-BRIEF.md and
# returning 200 to anyone who guessed the path. Add the folder here the same
# day a new one lands, and never park a working document inside a route
# directory like the-build/.
The Build page/
Greece Retreat/
# Renamed from `Retreats/`. A draft folder whose name differs from a route
# directory only by case is a trap: this project is uploaded from a
# case-insensitive filesystem, so `Retreats/` here could have taken the
# real `/retreats/` page out of the deploy with it.
Retreat drafts/
# Both arrived mid-session on 26 August 2026 and were built on 26 August into
# /a-sounding/ and /the-letters/. The wireframes stay excluded: they carry an
# annotation layer, a notes toggle and, in the Letters draft, a live HoneyBook
# widget pointed at the retired Collective form.
#
# Checked against the case-insensitive-filesystem trap above: lowercased,
# `a sounding` and `the letters page` are neither of them `a-sounding` or
# `the-letters`, so neither draft can take a route directory out of the
# deploy with it. Keep it that way when renaming either.
A Sounding/
The Letters Page/
# Arrived 26 August 2026, 19:07, mid-session. Excluded before anything else
# was done with it, per the rule above: an unexcluded folder in this root is
# served, and the build brief was once live at a guessable path.
the questions/
# Arrived 26 August 2026, later the same evening. Excluded on sight, same
# rule. It looks like the answer to the privacy/terms cutover trap in
# HANDOFF section 7.3, but it is a working document until something is
# built from it, and a working document in this root is a served document.
Privacy terms page/
